# C9D Identity — @c9d/auth-core (server primitives)

## Use

Use `@c9d/auth-core` for framework-neutral server auth logic:

- env contract resolution and fail-fast validation
- OIDC discovery retrieval
- PKCE/state/session payload helpers
- token exchange request body composition

## Required env contract

- `C9D_IDENTITY_URL` (or `NEXT_PUBLIC_C9D_IDENTITY_URL`)
- `C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID` (or `NEXT_PUBLIC_C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID`)
- `C9D_SESSION_SECRET`
- `APP_BASE_URL` or `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`

Optional:

- `C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` (server-only; confidential clients)

Never define `NEXT_PUBLIC_C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET`.

## Security

- Keep `C9D_SESSION_SECRET` and `C9D_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET` out of client bundles.
- Keep authorization code token exchange server-side.
- Generate session secret with `openssl rand -base64 32`.

